## Base member reference

The 8 locked base members are hard-coded in `base_members[]`. They are never removed. `run-council` uses
this list to expand the `all-base` dispatch token.

| Member | Default model | Dispatch topics (required) |
|---|---|---|
| `security-guard` | sonnet | `deviation`, `tier`, `inventory`, `spec`, `g6`, `import` |
| `framework-guard` | haiku | `deviation`, `tier`, `inventory`, `spec`, `g6`, `import` |
| `code-reviewer` | sonnet | `deviation`, `tier`, `inventory`, `spec`, `g6`, `import` |
| `safety-guard` | sonnet | `deviation`, `tier`, `inventory`, `spec`, `g6`, `import` |
| `migration-guard` | haiku | `g6`, `import`, `schema-lock` |
| `deploy-guard` | haiku | `g6`, `import` |
| `schema-guard` | haiku | `deviation`, `spec`, `g6`, `import`, `schema-lock` |
| `adr-guard` | haiku | `tier`, `spec`, `g6`, `import`, `cross-domain`, `capability-surface` |

## Required dispatch topics reference

The 6 topics required by `council.schema.json → dispatch_rules.topic_to_members`:

| Topic | Minimum members (pre-conditional injection) |
|---|---|
| `deviation` | `code-reviewer`, `safety-guard`, `schema-guard` |
| `tier` | `code-reviewer`, `adr-guard` |
| `inventory` | `code-reviewer`, `framework-guard` |
| `spec` | `code-reviewer`, `adr-guard`, `schema-guard` |
| `g6` | all 8 base members (`all-base`) |
| `import` | all 8 base members (`all-base`) |

## Conditional member reference

| Member | Enabled when | Default model | Topics added to |
|---|---|---|---|
| `cascade-developer` | `questionnaire.has_cascade OR scan.has_cascade` | sonnet | `deviation`, `tier`, `inventory`, `g6`, `import` |
| `mobile-ux` | `questionnaire.has_mobile OR scan.has_mobile` | haiku | `deviation`, `inventory`, `g6`, `import` |
| `payroll-engine-expert` | `scan.has_payroll` | sonnet | `inventory`, `spec`, `g6`, `import` |

